G:10 learned tensors/1390 values; both skip joins retain two inputs.
\image(figures/pix2pix_architecture.svg)
// result_end
\caption(The trace executes the canonical source-only generator and retains both inputs of each concatenation. Learned transposed convolutions replace no operation with nearest upsampling.)
\alttext(An executed seven-stage28-to14-to7-to14-to28 U-Net trace shows the encoder skip and the direct source skip at their actual concatenations.)

> Prepare genuine paired fitting, validation and test images natively

`prepare_example_data("mnist-assets",...)` creates the canonical saliency pools:
1000 fitting,200 validation and200 test rows. `LoadSaliency` keeps unit-range
Float32 images, labels and original source IDs. `quantized_sobel_edges` constructs
conditions independently for each image with the fixed integer transform above.
There is no fitting of edge thresholds or use of held-out labels to build features.
The first fitting example of each label0 through9 appears below, condition then
target. The complete original pools/conditions/labels/IDs are saved in data.npz.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pix2pix_pools.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& file) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : n::load_npz(file))
    a.emplace(k, v);
  return a;
}
std::vector<std::int64_t> Balanced(const n::Tensor& labels) {
  auto                      values = labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) {
    auto it = std::find(values.begin(), values.end(), c);
    if (it == values.end())
      throw std::runtime_error("all ten preview classes");
    rows.push_back(it - values.begin());
  }
  return rows;
}
void Grid(
    const std::string&               path,
    const std::vector<n::Tensor>&    columns,
    const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) {
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
  for (auto row : rows)
    for (const auto& column : columns)
      panels.push_back(n::take_rows(column, {row}));
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(panels, 0), path, columns.size(), 0, 1, 4, 220 / 255., 3);
}
int main() {
  auto path = std::filesystem::path(dm::datasets::data_home()) / "saliency";
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", path.parent_path());
  auto pools = m::LoadSaliency(path);
  auto edges = n::quantized_sobel_edges(pools[0].images);
  Grid("build/pix2pix_pools.png", {edges, pools[0].images}, Balanced(pools[0].labels));
}
```
